Now, each can of tomatoes is 16 ounces. So how many cans does 64 ounces of tomatoes amount to? Well, 64 divided by 16 is 4. So she used 4 cans of tomatoes. And each can contains three tomatoes. So 4 cans times 3 tomatoes per can would be 12 tomatoes. 

