But let me think again. Is there any chance that the problem is referring to something else? Like, maybe the loss of volume is per can or something else? But the problem says "when Freda cooks canned tomatoes into sauce, they lose half their volume." So regardless of the number of cans, when she cooks them, they lose half their volume. So if she uses, say, 4 cans, each can is 16 ounces, so total original volume is 4*16=64 ounces. Then when cooked, that becomes 32 ounces. 

