Alternatively, maybe I need to check if the 32 ounces of sauce is after cooking, so original volume is 64 ounces. Therefore, how many cans is that? 64 divided by 16 is 4 cans. So yes, same answer. 

I think that's right. Let me check if there's any other way this could be interpreted. For example, if the problem had said that each can, when cooked, becomes half a can, but no. The problem says that the tomatoes lose half their volume. So starting with 16 ounces, ending with 8 ounces. So each can contributes 8 ounces of sauce. 

